INT. CORPORATE ESCAPE ROOM - AFTERNOON

A fake Egyptian tomb: plywood hieroglyphs, a papier-mache sarcophagus, a countdown clock glowing red. 12:00. 11:59.

The team stands in a huddle. LONNIE KASPRZAK (40s, VP of Synergy, polo shirt, lanyard) holds a golden key. DEEPA MURTHY-LANGE (30s, project manager, clipboard) studies a wall of glyphs. WILHELM TSAI (20s, junior analyst, vest, eager) pokes the sarcophagus.

LONNIE
Okay team, I have a feeling about this key.

DEEPA
It's a prop, Lonnie.

WILHELM
It could be the key to the sarcophagus!

LONNIE
It could be the key to success.

DEEPA
It could be the key to nothing.

WILHELM
I think I found a latch!

LONNIE
Wilhelm, don't touch the mummy.

DEEPA
Lonnie, he is not a mummy, he's a Styrofoam sarcophagus.

WILHELM
It's a very good sarcophagus.

The clock ticks. 10:42.

LONNIE
Deepa, translate the glyphs.

DEEPA
They say, "This is not real."

LONNIE
Interesting.

WILHELM
Maybe it's a riddle!

LONNIE
Everything is a riddle, Wilhelm.

Deepa rips the clipboard off its hook. Lonnie shoves the key into the sarcophagus lock. It turns with a satisfying click. The lid hisses open.

Inside: a rubber snake and a plastic trophy.

LONNIE (CONT'D)
(whispering)
We did it.

DEEPA
We finished a team-building exercise.

WILHELM
We won?

LONNIE
We won!

They scream. High-five. Hug. Deepa exhales, a real laugh breaking through her professional mask.

A buzzer sounds. The red clock flashes. 00:00.

DEEPA
It's over.

LONNIE
Was it ever really about winning?

WILHELM
Yes.
